# Stalwart — example bootstrap config (production reference)

This is a **reference template**, not something to mount on first boot: a fresh
container auto-generates a valid `config.toml` into `/etc/stalwart`. Use this template
when you want a PostgreSQL backend and tailored listeners from the start. After first
boot, most runtime configuration is managed in the admin UI.

Replace every `<PLACEHOLDER>` before deploying.

```toml
[server]
hostname = "mx1.guidedstepswellness.com"
max-connections = 8192

[server.tls]
enable = true
implicit = true
certificate = "file:///opt/stalwart/certs/fullchain.pem"
private-key = "file:///opt/stalwart/certs/privkey.pem"

[authentication.fallback-admin]
user = "admin"
secret = "<ADMIN_PASSWORD>"

# --- Listeners ---
[server.listener.https]
bind = "[::]:443"
protocol = "http"
tls.implicit = true

[server.listener.http]
bind = "[::]:8080"
protocol = "http"

[server.listener.smtp]
bind = "[::]:25"
protocol = "smtp"

[server.listener.submissions]
bind = "[::]:465"
protocol = "smtp"
tls.implicit = true

[server.listener.submission]
bind = "[::]:587"
protocol = "smtp"

[server.listener.imap]
bind = "[::]:143"
protocol = "imap"

[server.listener.imaptls]
bind = "[::]:993"
protocol = "imap"
tls.implicit = true

[server.listener.sieve]
bind = "[::]:4190"
protocol = "managesieve"

# --- Anti-abuse (keep these high so you do not ban your own proxy) ---
[server.auto-ban.auth-failures]
rate = "10000/1d"
[server.auto-ban.abuse]
rate = "10000/1d"
[server.auto-ban.loiter]
rate = "10000/1d"
[server.auto-ban.scan]
rate = "10000/1d"

# --- Product store: PostgreSQL (alternative to default RocksDB) ---
[store.postgresql_cluster]
type = "postgresql"
host = "postgres"
port = 5432
database = "stalwart_mail"
user = "<STALWART_DB_USER>"
password = "<STALWART_DB_PASSWORD>"
pool.max-connections = 10

[storage]
data = "postgresql_cluster"
blob = "postgresql_cluster"
fts = "postgresql_cluster"
lookup = "postgresql_cluster"
directory = "postgresql_cluster"
```

## Notes
- The official Docker image in this repo instead uses named volumes (RocksDB) for local
  development; switch to this template for production hosting.
- When the outbound path migrates to a relay inside Stalwart (not the MVP), a relay
  route looks like:
  `queue.route.relay.type = "relay"`, `protocol = "smtp"`, `address`, `port`,
  `auth.username`, `auth.secret`.
- Gate the admin ports (443/8080) behind the security boundary; they must not be
  published to every application.